From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Stoffel <stoffel.thomas.ryan@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 21:28:22 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] startup: open the Agents window at launch

The Agents window is wisp's main UI (decision record 0011). Started with
no file or folder arguments, no --new-window, and no macOS open-file
event, wisp opens it instead of restoring or opening an editor window.
When the dock reopens the app with no visible window, it opens the
Agents window instead of an empty editor window.

`wisp <folder>` and `wisp <file>` never reach either branch, so they
still open the editor window, and --new-window still opens an empty
one. A --remote launch keeps upstream's behavior, since the Agents
window has no remote authority.

diff --git a/src/vs/code/electron-main/app.ts b/src/vs/code/electron-main/app.ts
index b9a22c34f22106d9343ef49aeee9e3ae54bf8978..52e797cd498096ddd1bf16505c6f557a56034af2 100644
--- a/src/vs/code/electron-main/app.ts
+++ b/src/vs/code/electron-main/app.ts
@@ -558,7 +558,7 @@ export class CodeApplication extends Disposable {
 
 			// Mac only event: open new window when we get activated
 			if (!hasVisibleWindows) {
-				await this.windowsMainService?.openEmptyWindow({ context: OpenContext.DOCK });
+				await this.windowsMainService?.openAgentsWindow({ context: OpenContext.DOCK, cli: this.environmentMainService.args });
 			}
 		});
 
@@ -1605,6 +1605,10 @@ export class CodeApplication extends Disposable {
 					// remoteAuthority: will be determined based on macOpenFiles
 				});
 			}
+
+			if (!remoteAuthority) {
+				return windowsMainService.openAgentsWindow({ context, cli: args, initialStartup: true });
+			}
 		}
 
 		// default: read paths from cli
